{"key":"enterprise/T1202","id":"T1202","name":"Indirect Command Execution","domain":"enterprise","level":"technique","parent_id":null,"tactics":["stealth"],"platforms":["Windows"],"environments":["cloud-hosted-endpoint","onprem"],"environment_basis":"project_taxonomy_from_upstream_platforms","summary":"Adversaries may abuse utilities that allow for command execution to bypass security restrictions that limit the use of command-line interpreters. Various Windows utilities may be used to execute commands, possibly without invoking cmd. For example, Forfiles, the Program Compatibility Assistant (`pcalua.exe`), components of the Windows Subsystem for Linux (WSL), `Scriptrunner.exe`, as well as other utilities may invoke the execution of programs…","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1202","source_stix_id":"attack-pattern--3b0e52ce-517a-4614-a523-1bd5deef6c5e","source_modified":"2026-05-12T15:12:00.628Z","source_object_version":"2.0","telemetry":{"status":"mapped","components":[{"id":"DC0039","name":"File Creation","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0039","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--2b3bfe19-d59a-460d-93bb-2f546adc2d2c","page":"telemetry/DC0039/"},{"id":"DC0082","name":"Network Connection Creation","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0082","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--181a9f8c-c780-4f1f-91a8-edb770e904ba","page":"telemetry/DC0082/"},{"id":"DC0032","name":"Process Creation","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0032","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--3d20385b-24ef-40e1-9f56-f39750379077","page":"telemetry/DC0032/"}],"strategies":[{"id":"DET0200","name":"Indirect Command Execution – Windows utility abuse behavior chain","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0200","stix_id":"x-mitre-detection-strategy--f3cc2f0f-c657-4453-90a8-d7c9a59d6e37","relationship_id":"relationship--8bb1b5ae-824e-41f2-b3a3-f852e8c9bffe"}],"analytics":[{"id":"AN0576","name":"Analytic 0576","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0200#AN0576","guidance":"Cause→effect chain: (1) A user or service launches an indirection utility (e.g., forfiles.exe, pcalua.exe, wsl.exe, scriptrunner.exe, ssh.exe with -o ProxyCommand/LocalCommand). (2) That utility spawns a secondary program/command (PowerShell, cmd, msiexec, regsvr32, curl, arbitrary EXE) and/or opens outbound network connections. (3) Optional precursor modification of SSH config to persist LocalCommand/ProxyCommand. Correlate process creation, command/script content, file access to %USERPROFILE%\\.ssh\\config, and network connections from the utility or its child.","platforms":["Windows"],"strategy_id":"DET0200"}],"log_sources":[{"component_id":"DC0032","component":"Process Creation","name":"WinEventLog:Sysmon","channel":"EventCode=1","platforms":["Windows"],"analytic_id":"AN0576","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0200#AN0576","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0032/"},{"component_id":"DC0082","component":"Network Connection Creation","name":"WinEventLog:Sysmon","channel":"EventCode=3, 22","platforms":["Windows"],"analytic_id":"AN0576","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0200#AN0576","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0082/"},{"component_id":"DC0039","component":"File Creation","name":"WinEventLog:Sysmon","channel":"EventCode=11","platforms":["Windows"],"analytic_id":"AN0576","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0200#AN0576","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0039/"}],"unresolved_references":[],"basis":"ATT&CK detects relationship → detection strategy → analytic → log-source component reference","planning_inputs":[],"visibility":"source_mapped","planning_references":[],"references":[{"id":"DC0039","name":"File Creation","tag":"File Creation","page":"telemetry/DC0039/","kind":"attack_comp